        <mxCell id="c174" value="Rule on A4:I11, A4 active: &lt;b&gt;=ABS($I4)&amp;gt;$B$14&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="22" y="454" width="500" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c175" value="&lt;i&gt;Rows 1 and 2 hold the title and the period labels. With the threshold typed as one point instead of two, four product types (BKC, CON, NGT, SDB) change their share by more than one point, the falls and the rises alike, so their rows are shaded across all nine columns and B15 counts them. At two points no row is shaded and the count is zero, which the rule alone cannot tell from a rule that never fires. Outlined: the threshold and the count.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="482" width="860" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
